 src/terminal_app.rs  |  42 ++-
 src/ui.rs            | 593 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 src/ui_harness.rs    |  28 +-
 tests/ui_harness.rs  |  76 ++++++
 5 files changed, 688 insertions(+), 59 deletions(-)

diff --git a/docs/architecture.md b/docs/architecture.md
index e0a7f0a..4023865 100644
--- a/docs/architecture.md
+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -305,6 +305,14 @@ When an agent chat is selected in command mode, `/` focuses the chat, seeds the
 `/`, and enters insert mode so `/status`-style input submits through the same selected-agent chat
 path.
 
+Command mode also supports Vim-style visual selection in the terminal panes. `v` starts a character
+selection, `V` starts a line selection, and Ctrl-V starts a rectangular block selection. The selection
+anchor uses the focused pane: the left pane anchors on the rendered control row for the selected
+agent or command surface, and the right pane anchors on the visible chat cursor row. While a visual
+selection is active, `h`/`j`/`k`/`l` and the arrow keys move the selection cursor. `y` yanks the
+selected text and `Y` yanks it as line text; `TerminalUi` emits an OSC 52 clipboard sequence on the
+next render frame and shows a short copied-selection status notice.
+
 The terminal app maps a session to a left-pane `READY` marker when the controller exposes no loading
 state for that session. `TerminalUi` queues one terminal bell when a chat transitions into the ready
 state and renders ready rows in reverse video so they remain highlighted until the chat becomes busy
